James encountered a compilation error in his code: "C-style cast from 'ifstream' to 'istream' uses deleted function." The issue arose from trying to use a C-style cast on an `ifstream`. I explained that copying streams isn't generally allowed and recommended a fix by directly passing the `ifstream` object to `getline`, since it natively accepts `ifstream` as an `istream`. The corrected line of code should be `getline(file, line);`, which resolves the error. I also advised checking if the `file` was properly opened and to look for other potential issues in the code.
